# Project Conventions — Engineering Domain

## Code Style
- **Python**: Ruff (line-length=100), Pydantic v2, AnyIO-only
- **Imports**: Absolute imports; no relative imports in src/omega
- **Types**: Full type hints; `from __future__ import annotations`
- **Errors**: Typed OmegaError hierarchy; no bare except
- **Async**: AnyIO only; no asyncio direct usage

## File Organization
```
src/omega/
├── oracle/           # Core engine (Oracle, ModelGateway, EntityRegistry)
├── memory/           # MemoryStore, sqlite-vec, hybrid search
├── cli/              # Typer CLI (oracle_cli.py)
├── observability/    # Trace IDs, events, metrics
├── governance/       # Config resolver, budget guard
├── workers/          # Background workers (YouTube, research)
└── mcp_servers/      # Omega Hub (modularized)
```

## Naming Conventions
- **Classes**: PascalCase (`ModelGateway`, `EntityRegistry`)
- **Functions**: snake_case (`generate`, `find_by_domain`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_LIMIT`)
- **Files**: snake_case (`model_gateway.py`, `entity_registry.py`)

## Testing Conventions
- **Contract tests**: `tests/contract/test_*.py` — verify API boundaries
- **Integration tests**: `tests/integration/test_*.py` — end-to-end
- **Unit tests**: `tests/test_*.py` — isolated units
- **Benchmarks**: `tests/benchmarks/test_*.py` — performance

## Documentation Conventions
- **Architecture**: `docs/architecture/` — system design
- **Strategy**: `docs/strategy/` — planning, decisions, roadmaps
- **Research**: `docs/research/` — deep dives, evidence
- **Legacy**: `docs/legacy/` — mined patterns from old stacks